<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Taizu of Jin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1068–1123</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Wanyan Aguda, Aguda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wanyan Aguda was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-jin-dynasty">Jurchen Jin dynasty</a> and its first emperor, known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song">Taizu</a>, ruling from 1115 to 1123. Chief of the Wanyan clan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a>, he rebelled against the Khitan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty</a> in 1114, proclaimed the Jin in 1115 and won a series of victories that brought down the Liao, completed by his brother after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-jin.jpg" alt="Emperor Taizu of Jin" width="320" height="468" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wanggiyan_Aguda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
